In this world,

555
00:40:06,679 --> 00:40:09,120
who doesn't want a better life?

556
00:40:10,719 --> 00:40:12,519
I'm greedy, too.

557
00:40:13,519 --> 00:40:15,720
But our forebears taught us,

558
00:40:16,159 --> 00:40:19,240
"A gentleman acquires
wealth by honorable means."

559
00:40:19,400 --> 00:40:21,919
You can't trample on others

560
00:40:21,920 --> 00:40:25,519
just because you want a better life.

561
00:40:35,039 --> 00:40:37,240
I don't think
I did anything wrong, either.

562
00:40:42,199 --> 00:40:43,720
But why

563
00:40:46,559 --> 00:40:48,320
do I still feel so awful?

564
00:40:54,159 --> 00:40:55,640
Because...

565
00:40:57,800 --> 00:40:58,919
you...

566
00:41:00,159 --> 00:41:02,320
are a good person.

567
00:41:05,740 --> 00:41:12,260
♪If you're a lone traveler
returning through the snow♪

568
00:41:18,400 --> 00:41:20,280
I'm a good person...

569
00:41:24,780 --> 00:41:28,900
♪If you're the silent fragrance
of a secluded orchid♪

570
00:41:33,039 --> 00:41:34,600
I like hearing that.

571
00:41:35,559 --> 00:41:36,558
Say it some more...

572
00:41:36,559 --> 00:41:41,660
♪Deep within the lights lies
a truth that came too late♪

573
00:41:43,940 --> 00:41:48,980
♪Even if these trials
consume my whole life♪

574
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:50,078
You're really drunk.

575
00:41:50,079 --> 00:41:53,419
♪I'll only return
to the moment our fate began♪

576
00:41:53,420 --> 00:41:57,059
♪I've searched and searched,
wandering in circles♪

577
00:41:57,060 --> 00:42:00,019
♪Yet I can never mend that old dream♪

578
00:42:00,020 --> 00:42:02,979
♪Leaving only regret behind♪

579
00:42:02,980 --> 00:42:07,860
♪Thankfully, these trials
have spared me a lifetime♪

580
00:42:07,900 --> 00:42:13,300
♪In this life and the next,
it will always be you♪

581
00:42:13,700 --> 00:42:21,980
♪I only pray that fate
lets us meet sooner♪

582
00:42:35,940 --> 00:42:38,780
(Your pay and provisions
come from the people's toil.)

583
00:42:41,320 --> 00:42:44,280
Liang Yu, Commander
of the Shence Garrison,

584
00:42:44,760 --> 00:42:46,600
has enjoyed His Majesty's favor,

585
00:42:47,039 --> 00:42:49,038
yet gave no thought
to serving the realm.

586
00:42:49,039 --> 00:42:50,919
He colluded with Dai Rong

587
00:42:51,039 --> 00:42:53,120
and formed a faction for personal gain.

588
00:42:53,440 --> 00:42:54,919
He disregarded the greater good

589
00:42:54,920 --> 00:42:56,720
and pursued his own interests.

590
00:42:57,239 --> 00:43:01,359
He is hereby stripped
of office and imprisoned.

591
00:43:05,060 --> 00:43:07,780
=Against the Current=
(Next Episode's Preview)

592
00:43:08,056 --> 00:43:10,350
First Madam, Young Master,
for all you've done for us,

593
00:43:10,360 --> 00:43:12,759
our whole family will always
remember your kindness.

594
00:43:12,760 --> 00:43:14,479
Every day,
we'll kowtow to the Bodhisattva

595
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:16,100
and pray
for the Bodhisattva's blessings.

596
00:43:16,110 --> 00:43:17,959
May First Madam
be blessed with many descendants

597
00:43:17,960 --> 00:43:19,384
and an ever-flourishing family line.

598
00:43:19,416 --> 00:43:21,510
May Young Master
be blessed with a destined match

599
00:43:21,519 --> 00:43:22,919
and a marriage made in heaven.

600
00:43:26,239 --> 00:43:27,039
Yes.

601
00:43:27,079 --> 00:43:29,640
Every day, we'll kowtow
and burn incense to the Bodhisattva

602
00:43:29,679 --> 00:43:30,558
and pray
for the Bodhisattva's blessings.

603
00:43:30,559 --> 00:43:31,158
May...

604
00:43:31,159 --> 00:43:32,879
May the Bodhisattva bless you.

605
00:43:34,440 --> 00:43:35,999
You certainly have a way with words.

606
00:43:36,440 --> 00:43:37,640
What you said

607
00:43:37,760 --> 00:43:39,680
is exactly what
First Madam and I wish for.

608
00:43:40,392 --> 00:43:41,870
May your auspicious words come true.

609
00:43:41,880 --> 00:43:43,120
I hope that someday,

610
00:43:43,230 --> 00:43:44,984
everything will turn out
just as we wish.

611
00:44:01,461 --> 00:44:05,581
♪Spring slips from the
branches once more♪

612
00:44:08,421 --> 00:44:12,941
♪Flowers bloom unseen,
as they have before♪

613
00:44:14,221 --> 00:44:18,141
♪All the joys and sorrows come and go♪

614
00:44:18,821 --> 00:44:21,581
♪While loss leaves winter in the heart♪

615
00:44:22,301 --> 00:44:24,621
♪Though all the world may fade♪

616
00:44:24,621 --> 00:44:27,701
♪Time rolls on as
countless lives rush by♪

617
00:44:29,221 --> 00:44:33,461
♪Night winds wander
through the halls of long ago♪

618
00:44:36,381 --> 00:44:40,541
♪No page could hold the
longing words can never show♪

619
00:44:42,341 --> 00:44:45,901
♪Every joy and sorrow
in this fleeting life♪

620
00:44:45,901 --> 00:44:49,461
♪Fades into the past
as new wounds rise♪

621
00:44:50,261 --> 00:44:55,941
♪While whispers of perfume
linger beneath the eaves♪

622
00:44:56,301 --> 00:45:00,621
♪Let the cold wind rage,
let the wild rain fall♪

623
00:45:00,981 --> 00:45:03,941
♪Let sorrow spill like shadows over all♪

624
00:45:03,941 --> 00:45:07,701
♪Let love fall to pieces,
let old anger burn away♪

625
00:45:07,701 --> 00:45:10,581
♪Let the past die with yesterday♪

626
00:45:10,581 --> 00:45:14,661
♪One last fire, one last cup of wine♪

627
00:45:14,661 --> 00:45:18,021
♪And silver moonlight to
guide me through the night♪

628
00:45:18,021 --> 00:45:21,781
♪Let beginnings fade
as endings come to call♪

629
00:45:21,781 --> 00:45:25,781
♪From this endless dream,
there's no return at all♪

630
00:45:26,541 --> 00:45:30,701
♪Let the cold wind rage,
let the wild rain fall♪

631
00:45:30,701 --> 00:45:34,141
♪Let sorrow spill like shadows over all♪

632
00:45:34,141 --> 00:45:37,781
♪Let love fall to pieces,
let old anger burn away♪

633
00:45:37,781 --> 00:45:40,661
♪Let the past die with yesterday♪

634
00:45:40,661 --> 00:45:44,741
♪One last fire, one last cup of wine♪

635
00:45:44,741 --> 00:45:48,101
♪And silver moonlight to
guide me through the night♪

636
00:45:48,101 --> 00:45:51,741
♪Let beginnings fade
as endings come to call♪

637
00:45:51,741 --> 00:45:59,541
♪From this endless dream,
there's no return at all♪

